    "description": "Financial Analyst\nProgram Analyst\nSharePoint Developer\n\n•\tDesigned a SharePoint-based contract acquisition tool used by the FAA to help support the contract acquisition process of the National Airspace System Integration Support Contract (NISC-III), a performance-based contract worth $1.4 billion over 10 years.\n\n•\tIdentified a regularly-occurring, manual process performed by the FAA that could be improved through electronic means and designed a SharePoint-based contract performance evaluation tool to facilitate the bi-annual evaluation of the task order management and technical achievement of the NISC contractor.  \n\n•\tDesigned, tested, and served as web content manager and developer of the NISC program’s web intranet in collaboration with a team of developers, analysts, and FAA clients.  \n\n•\tSupported the development of a ColdFusion and Oracle-based contract management system (KITT) by working in a team to create and define the business rules and logic for the system, testing and error reporting of the system, serving as the site administrator, and fulfilling help desk functions.  \n\n•\tResearched and created customer satisfaction surveys to determine ways to improve program support to customers, directly resulting in improved participation in monthly teleconferences.  Research was also used to generate new ideas for task order performance metrics, an ongoing NISC program initiative of integrating quantitive metrics in performance-based contracting.\n\n•\tProvided invoice analysis, financial tracking and projections, requisitions creation, coordination of training, and other contract administration duties for FAA NISC contract using Microsoft Office Suite, KITT (NISC Contract Management System), eLMS (DOT Learning Management System), PRISM (FAA Procurement Management System), DELPHI (DOT Accounting System)",
