    "description": "•\tPerform web publishing and content management tasks on a daily basis for the Office of the Comptroller of the Currency (OCC) as part of a web content management team\n\n•\tWeb publishing and content management tasks include:\n\no\tDeveloping, coding, and testing web pages using the Percussion Rhythmyx Content Management System (CMS), HTML/XHTML, CSS, JavaScript, and ASP for the five OCC web sites that are managed by the team.  They consist of the public sites, OCC.gov and HelpWithMyBank.gov, employee intranet, OCC.net, and bank examiners sites, BankNet.gov and Examiner’s Library (EL.occ).  \no\tUsing the Remedy-based ticketing system to track, manage, and record work requests in coordination with web liaisons and web content management team members\no\tPublishing and rescinding OCC news issuances on OCC.gov and EL.occ\no\tRSS updates on OCC.gov\no\tCreating emails using the Lyris email subscription service for broadcast to the OCC list servers\no\tRunning and creating customized WebTrends web metrics reports\no\tConversion of formatted publications to web based equivalents using XML tools such as Arbortext\no\tPeer review of team members’ work\no\tImage creation and editing in Adobe Photoshop\n\n•\tCollaboration projects with web liaisons and web content management team members involve:\no\tReviewing and testing web pages \no\tTroubleshooting coding issues\no\tSetting up meetings to discuss and propose solutions to clients’ needs\no\tSpecial projects coordinated with the OCC client\no\tManaging tasks and coordinating workloads to ensure that work is completed on time, eliminating any gaps in service, and enhancing responsiveness to clients",
